:: Test F2
{=

(metadata: "title", "Test F2 (multi-check gate)")

[[⇦ BACK->Pre-Test (NEW)]]
<br>
$cssColumnParent[

<!--initialize temp vars-->
(set: _linkText to "Multi-check gate link test.")
(set: _req to (dm:))
(set: _pocketName to "inv")
(set: _spend to false)
(set: _chance to 90)

<!--explanation of test-->
$cssColumnChild[

<!--special colored text-->
(set: _color to (color: white+green))

Testing the macro [`($funcMultiCheckGate:)`].
<br>
It takes the following arguments:
(box:"X", 3)[<ol>
<li>str-type _color[`_linkText`],</li>
<li>str-type _color[`_pocketName`],</li>
<li>dm-type _color[`_thingList`],</li>
<li>boolean-type _color[`_spend`],</li>
<li>num-type _color[`_chance`],</li>
<li>codehook-type _color[`_addCode`],</li>
<li>str-type _color[`_gotoSuccess`],</li>
<li>str-type _color[`_gotoFailure`],</li>
</ol>]
<br>
The most important argument is the _color[`_thingList` (dm)]. For this test, we fill it with the content below:

<ol>
<li>(link-rerun: "List of papers.")[{
    (set: _linkText to "Do you have your papers?")
    (set: _pocketName to "inv")
    (set: _req to (dm: "permitAskava", 1, "identityReceipt", 1, "universityCertificate", 1))
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]</li>

<li>(link-rerun: "An ID is fine.")[{
    (set: _linkText to "Show you ID.")
    (set: _pocketName to "inv")
    (set: _req to (dm: "identityReceipt", 1))
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]</li>

<li>(link-rerun: "List of attributes.")[{
    (set: _linkText to "Do you have the right attributes?")
    (set: _pocketName to "att")
    (set: _req to (dm: "at", 10, "ab", 20, "zam", 12, "vigorous", 1))
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]</li>

<li>(link-rerun: "Check for wounds (temporary effect).")[{
    (set: _linkText to "Are you doubly wounded?")
    (set: _pocketName to "temp")
    (set: _req to (dm: "wound", 2,))
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]</li>

<li>(link-rerun: "Spend mode?")[{
    (if: _spend is false)[(set: _spend to true)]
    (else:)[(set: _spend to false)]
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?spend)
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]` `Currently: [_spend[Spending](else:)[NOT spending]]<spend|</li>


<li>(link-rerun: "Change chance.")[{
    (dialog: bind _chance, "What are the chances of success?", "0", "20", "50", "70", "90", "100")
    (set: _chance to (num: _chance))
    (t8n: "dissolve")(rerun: ?test)
}]</li>
</ol>


]<!--end child-->

<!--test-->
$cssColumnChild[
<ol>
[<li>($funcMultiCheckGate: _linkText, _pocketName, _req, _spend, _chance, [], "Test F2 (Success)", "Test F2 (Failure)")</li>]<test|
<li>Just trying to see how the above will appear when put in a list. Apparently, line-height: 1.6 works very well.</li>
</ol>


]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->


:: Test F2 (Success)

Yay! Success!
<br>
(link: "Back")[(goto: "Test F2")]


:: Test F2 (Failure)

Aw, failure.
<br>
(link: "Back")[(goto: "Test F2")]